# Review is required on everything while there is one maintainer (GOVERNANCE.md),
# so this file is less about routing than about making the high-consequence
# paths impossible to merge past by accident. When a second maintainer arrives,
# GOVERNANCE.md's two-maintainer rules take effect and these lines get owners
# that are not the same person.
#
# Spelled as a user rather than as @valqore/qed-maintainers on purpose: GitHub
# ignores a CODEOWNERS line naming a team that does not exist, and does it
# quietly, so the protection would read as present and be absent. That is the
# same failure mode as a compliance control nobody enforces.

*                                       @tunc-celik-valqore

# The frozen evidence format. A change here can invalidate records already in a
# customer's database, which is the one failure this project cannot walk back
# (ADR-0015).
/qed/core/evidence/                     @tunc-celik-valqore
/packages/qed-verify/                   @tunc-celik-valqore
/tests/evidence/fixtures/               @tunc-celik-valqore
/docs/evidence-format.md                @tunc-celik-valqore

# The decision path. `qed.core` imports no HTTP client, no socket and no model
